  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_03926b6b783b48b1825d378877a0d6f3",
      "statement": "The apps/billcollector package is a daemon that turns the cron batch job into a 24/7 daemon: an orchestrator spawns one subprocess per task run (sync Playwright), each run is pausable through a versioned control socket, and a machine-readable pause context is persisted for human (and future AI) intervention; the module deliberately avoids heavy imports so the UI process is the only one loading the web stack.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/billcollector/__init__.py#L1-L13",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ce3e382924f63261748e4b824ccda8e8e2084e7205300f88375716368ad95f24:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_69c6f38fe567493b929b120a47762660",
      "statement": "The daemon entrypoint is `python3 -m billcollector serve` (NiceGUI on port 8000 by default), which imports the INI files into the Task table on start, seeds the UI password hash from BC_UI_PASSWORD before serving, and `python3 -m billcollector run <task_id>` executes a single task run standalone; NiceGUI and Playwright are imported lazily per subcommand.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L170-L178",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6a256ba2744ad552312e3c5520ca263411ffdc657257d01b3dcf610260e2c486:"
