    {
      "id": "claim_4857522f5131454f810f17f1ba197588",
      "statement": "The post-download consumer hook slot (decision 14) is deliberately empty: CONSUMERS is an initially empty list, and the slot contract is that each appended callable is invoked as consume(download: dict) for every new (non-duplicate) download inside the runner subprocess so a slow consumer never blocks the UI/scheduler; the tracking machinery (per-task sha256 dedup, consumers must never break the run) is live in downloads.py, but no document consumer is implemented, so downstream DMS handoff still happens via the shared download folder.",
